From aff069f294d004e5be0dafb86de513593c4d2db1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:09:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VAX8300: the second KA820 runs (VAX 8300/8350
 multiprocessing)

SET KA1 ENABLE adds a second KA820 at VAXBI node 1 that executes: VAX/VMS
V4.4+ with the VMS/8300 multiprocessing key starts it with START/CPU
(attached processor, asymmetric multiprocessing).  Before, KA1 was only a
BI node; the RXCD start commands were stubs (#if VAX_MP, never defined),
so START/CPU ended with %SYSTEM-F-DEVOFFLINE (known issues 65).

CPU core (vax_cpu.c, vax_mmu.c/h, vax_defs.h; only with VAX_MP, which
only the 8200 defines; every other VAX simulator compiles as before):
- one context per processor (CPU_CTX: registers, PSL, the IPR copies),
  switched every CPU QUANTUM instructions (default 100) at an instruction
  boundary, so interlocked instructions stay atomic; one translation
  buffer per processor;
- simulated time runs with the primary's instructions only: in guest
  time both processors run at full speed (with THROTTLE 400K each);
- a secondary's HALT, CTRL/P or error halt stops only it (halt message
  ?nn / PC / >>> to the primary's RXCD); its jump to itself at IPL 31
  (VMS's park loop after STOP/CPU) is no infinite-loop stop; no host idle
  while a secondary runs;
- outside of execution the globals hold processor 0 (EXAMINE, DEPOSIT,
  SAVE); a stop during the secondary's turn prints its PC.

KA820 (vax820_ka.c, vax820_bi.c, vax820_stddev.c, vax820_defs.h):
- RXCD console commands I, D/G, S act on the secondary;
- BIIC IPINTR mask/destination/source registers; node private space
  2008 0000 maps the local BIIC (VMS's start code uses both);
- a secondary takes only its own clock, IPI, console output and
  software interrupts; device, RXCD, floppy and terminal interrupts go
  to the primary; KA1 has its own ICCS/NICR (ticking with the primary's
  calibrated timer);
- KA1 registers (EXAMINE KA1 PC, PSL, R0 ...), SHOW KA1 STATE, HELP KA1,
  SET KA1 DEBUG=RXCD;MP; SHOW CPU model VAX 8300 (8350) with KA1.

Tested with VMS V4.7 (DEFINE/SYSTEM/EXEC MP MP8SS): START/CPU, SHOW CPU
IDLE / EXECUTE, STOP/CPU, START/CPU again; two CPU-bound jobs at THROTTLE
400K in 12-13 s instead of 21 s; 8200 diagnostics (also with a switch
after every instruction), console RX50 and standalone BACKUP boot on the
single processor; diagnostics of the 780, 750, 730, 8600, 3900.

Applies after patches 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Suavtcc46vFhoyQ1F6AQu4
